    "q-86214": {
      "dom_id": "step-q86214",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14195873/assets/aefac5e84b9ea13ce039e4e2e04fda830be9ab9c17a62665ba5e5d3a7b7f6f68.png)\n\nWe need to create a cylindrical tin with no lid using $108\\pi \\,{cm}^{2}$ of a metal sheet. What is the radius $r$ of the cylinder that has the largest volume?",
      "worked_solution": "First, let $r$ be the radius and $h$ be the height of the cylinder.\n\nWe wish to maximize the volume\n\n$$\nV=\\pi {r}^{2}h.\n$$\n\nWe know that the surface area is fixed at $108\\pi \\,{cm}^{2},$ so we also have the constraint equation\n\n$$\n2\\pi rh+\\pi {r}^{2}=108\\pi .\n$$\n\nNow, by making $h$ the subject of the constraint equation, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\pi rh & =108\\pi -\\pi {r}^{2} \\\\ h & =\\frac{108\\pi -\\pi {r}^{2}}{2\\pi r} \\\\ h & =\\frac{108-{r}^{2}}{2r}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nPlugging the above into our expression for $V,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V(r) & =\\pi {r}^{2}\\times \\frac{108-{r}^{2}}{2r} \\\\ V(r) & =\\frac{(108r-{r}^{3})\\pi }{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe want to maximize $V,$ so we need to differentiate $V$ and set the derivative equal to zero. The derivative is \n\n$$\n{V}^{′}(r)=\\frac{(108-3{r}^{2})\\pi }{2}.\n$$\n\nSetting the derivative equal to zero and solving for $r$ gives a stationary point, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{V}^{′}(r) & =0 \\\\ \\frac{(108-3{r}^{2})\\pi }{2} & =0 \\\\ 108 & =3{r}^{2} \\\\ {r}^{2} & =36 \\\\ r & =6\\,\\text{cm}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that, in the last step, we only considered the positive root because the radius $r$ must be positive.\n\nFinally, we confirm that $r=6$ is a maximum using the second derivative test. The second derivative ${V}^{″}(r)$ is\n\n$$\n{V}^{″}(r)=\\frac{-6\\pi r}{2}=-3\\pi r,\n$$\n\nand we can see that ${V}^{″}(6)<0.$ So, the stationary point $r=6$ is indeed a maximum of $V(r).$\n\nTherefore, the cylinder with the largest volume has a radius of $r=6\\,\\text{cm}.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-86214-a",
